  type: ClusterIP

===== 5. Upgrade: scale up and switch to the production overlay =====

$ helm upgrade notes notes-chart -n helm-lab -f notes-chart/values-prod.yaml --wait --timeout 5m
Release "notes" has been upgraded. Happy Helming!
NAME: notes
LAST DEPLOYED: Wed Oct  7 20:43:16 2026
NAMESPACE: helm-lab
STATUS: deployed
REVISION: 2
DESCRIPTION: Upgrade complete
TEST SUITE: None
NOTES:
notes-chart 0.1.0 installed as release "notes".

Environment: production
Replicas:    4

Reach it from inside the cluster:

  kubectl -n helm-lab run tmp --rm -it --image=curlimages/curl:8.7.1 --restart=Never -- \
    curl -s http://notes-notes-chart:80

$ helm list -n helm-lab
NAME 	NAMESPACE	REVISION	UPDATED                             	STATUS  	CHART            	APP VERSION
notes	helm-lab 	2       	2026-10-07 20:43:16.405444 +0530 IST	deployed	notes-chart-0.1.0	1.0        

$ kubectl -n helm-lab get deploy -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,REPLICAS:.spec.replicas
NAME                REPLICAS
notes-notes-chart   4

$ kubectl -n helm-lab get pods --no-headers
notes-notes-chart-545958b9d6-6wn2f   1/1   Running       0     7s
notes-notes-chart-545958b9d6-bd7kl   1/1   Running       0     1s
notes-notes-chart-545958b9d6-cmrfc   1/1   Running       0     1s
notes-notes-chart-545958b9d6-xqwqm   1/1   Running       0     7s
notes-notes-chart-74df7d7674-sccjk   1/1   Terminating   0     9s
# the env var changed too, not just the replica count:

$ kubectl -n helm-lab rollout status deployment/notes-notes-chart --timeout=180s
deployment "notes-notes-chart" successfully rolled out

$ kubectl -n helm-lab exec notes-notes-chart-545958b9d6-6wn2f -- sh -c 'echo APP_ENV=$APP_ENV; echo BANNER=$BANNER'
APP_ENV=production
BANNER=notes app, production overlay

===== 6. Upgrade again, with a single --set override =====

$ helm upgrade notes notes-chart -n helm-lab -f notes-chart/values-prod.yaml --set replicaCount=3 --wait --timeout 5m
