===== 7. History and rollback =====

$ helm history notes -n helm-lab
REVISION	UPDATED                 	STATUS    	CHART            	APP VERSION	DESCRIPTION     
1       	Wed Oct  7 20:43:14 2026	superseded	notes-chart-0.1.0	1.0        	Install complete
2       	Wed Oct  7 20:43:16 2026	superseded	notes-chart-0.1.0	1.0        	Upgrade complete
3       	Wed Oct  7 20:43:23 2026	deployed  	notes-chart-0.1.0	1.0        	Upgrade complete
# roll back to revision 1, the original development values

$ helm rollback notes 1 -n helm-lab --wait --timeout 5m
Rollback was a success! Happy Helming!

$ helm history notes -n helm-lab
REVISION	UPDATED                 	STATUS    	CHART            	APP VERSION	DESCRIPTION     
1       	Wed Oct  7 20:43:14 2026	superseded	notes-chart-0.1.0	1.0        	Install complete
2       	Wed Oct  7 20:43:16 2026	superseded	notes-chart-0.1.0	1.0        	Upgrade complete
3       	Wed Oct  7 20:43:23 2026	superseded	notes-chart-0.1.0	1.0        	Upgrade complete
4       	Wed Oct  7 20:43:23 2026	deployed  	notes-chart-0.1.0	1.0        	Rollback to 1   

$ kubectl -n helm-lab get deploy -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,REPLICAS:.spec.replicas
NAME                REPLICAS
notes-notes-chart   2

$ kubectl -n helm-lab rollout status deployment/notes-notes-chart --timeout=180s
deployment "notes-notes-chart" successfully rolled out

$ kubectl -n helm-lab exec notes-notes-chart-74df7d7674-hpxmf -- sh -c 'echo APP_ENV=$APP_ENV; echo BANNER=$BANNER'
APP_ENV=development
BANNER=notes app, default values
# back to the development values, so the rollback really changed the pods
# rollback is recorded as a NEW revision, it does not erase history

